The "suffix array intervals" form a tree. The root corresponds to the empty prefix (all suffixes). Its children correspond to distinct first characters. The number of children is the alphabet size. Then each child corresponds to an interval in the SA. Recursively, the minimum alphabet size is the maximum number of children of any node in this interval tree, minimized over all valid interval trees consistent with the SA.

